# Backend service

Run `tsrust dev`, then open http://127.0.0.1:4318/ or
http://127.0.0.1:4318/api/greet/Ada.
Routes, shared state and middleware live in app/main.tsr. Reusable logic lives in
app/lib; tests live in app/tests. The greeting is public. Add authorization with
app.use before registering protected routes. No API settings belong in JSON.

Generate independent clients from checked source; the server need not be running:

    tsrust api generate --out js-client
    tsrust api generate --language rust --out rust-client

The generated http-api.json contract also works in another project:

    tsrust api generate --description http-api.json --out client

Clients include OpenAPI. Generation changes only marked client outputs; it never
adds server routes or exposes a description endpoint. Bring your own UI and call
the HTTP API. No frontend toolchain or dependency installation is required.
Run tsrust check, tsrust test and tsrust format --check before deploying.
